      "text": "75-year-old female presenting with headache with dizziness for 5 weeks. Character: throbbing at the back of the head; radiation: to the neck; aggravated by morning time; relieved by rest. Severity 7/10. Associated: palpitations, blurred vision. PMH: Hypertension for 3 years; Hypothyroidism for 3 years. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg; Levothyroxine 50 mcg. Allergy: penicillin. Family: asthma. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
